What this licence covers, and what it does not

It does not cover what the repository builds from. The emulator is 86Box
(https://86box.net, https://github.com/86Box/86Box), at the commit pinned in
extern/86box (the v6.0 release), under the GNU General Public License
version 2 or later. The parts of 86Box the package is built from carry other
free licences beside it, each listed with its text in
waterbox/package-licenses.json: ymfm (BSD 3-Clause), Berkeley SoftFloat 3e
with Bochs' extensions (BSD 3-Clause and SoftFloat 2 terms), Nuked OPL3 and
ESFMu (GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later), reSID-fp (GNU
General Public License 2 or later), MiniVHD, ayumi and cJSON (MIT), and the
LZW routines of Michael Dipperstein (GNU Lesser General Public License
version 3 or later), with which 86Box reads Teledisk (.td0) images saved
with the old compression.

Because of those LZW routines, the program in the built package,
86box.chimeraCore, is under the GNU General Public License version 3 or
later: 86Box's "or later" allows it, and the version 3 of the Lesser GPL
needs it. The same is true of 86Box's own published builds. (Leaving the
routines out would keep the package under version 2 or later and cost
those .td0 images; that choice is the project owner's, docs/PLAN.md.)

The tests build Sergey Kiselev's 8088 BIOS (GNU General Public License
version 3) and a stand-in character ROM from its font for the test machine.
Neither is in this repository or in the package.

No ROM, BIOS or firmware of any computer is in this repository or in the
package: a user supplies them. No game is in this repository or in the
package.
